        <mxCell id="c48" value="&lt;i&gt;Outlined: the join keyword, the only difference between the two tabs. Both show lines 87 to 89 of test L4 in Audit.sql, the join to the payments; the query selects the approved registers that have no payment. With LEFT JOIN it returns registers 1, 2646 and 5420. With INNER JOIN no register can lack a payment, so the same test returns no rows, the answer a clean population would give. Each grid is scrolled to its first three columns.&lt;/i&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;fontColor=#5D6D7E;fontStyle=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;spacing=2;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="0" y="334" width="860" height="57" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
